        "point": "natural number multiples only",
        "statement": "The scalar `n` in `n • x` ranges over `ℕ`, so all elements are non-negative integer multiples of `x`; negative multiples are excluded.",
        "note": "Consequence of using ℕ-scalar multiplication (nsmul) rather than ℤ-scalar multiplication."
      },
      {
        "point": "zero is always a member",
        "statement": "The identity element `0 = 0 • x` is always a member, as required for any additive submonoid.",
